### TITLE ###
FilterPreservesSelectionByOriginalIndex
### DESCRIPTION ###
Selections are keyed to the option list, not to the filtered view, so choosing
apple, narrowing to avocado, choosing that, and clearing the filter keeps both.
Keying by visible position instead would silently move a checkmark onto whatever
row happened to take that slot.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
apple
banana
avocado
cherry
### KEYS ###
space
"av"
space
ctrl-u
enter
### SELECTED ###
apple
avocado
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> [ ] apple
  [ ] banana
  [ ] avocado
  [ ] cherry
--- frame 1 (space) ---
Pick
> [x] apple
  [ ] banana
  [ ] avocado
  [ ] cherry
--- frame 2 (a) ---
Pick
/a
> [x] apple
  [ ] avocado
  [ ] banana
--- frame 3 (v) ---
Pick
/av
> [ ] avocado
--- frame 4 (space) ---
Pick
/av
> [x] avocado
--- frame 5 (ctrl-u) ---
Pick
> [x] apple
  [ ] banana
  [x] avocado
  [ ] cherry
--- frame 6 (enter) ---
Pick apple, avocado

### TITLE ###
SubmitWhileFilteredToEmpty
### DESCRIPTION ###
The filter narrows what is shown, not what is held. Submitting from a view with
no matches still returns the selection made before the filter was typed.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
apple
banana
### KEYS ###
space
"z"
enter
### SELECTED ###
apple
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> [ ] apple
  [ ] banana
--- frame 1 (space) ---
Pick
> [x] apple
  [ ] banana
--- frame 2 (z) ---
Pick
/z
  (no matches - backspace to widen)
--- frame 3 (enter) ---
Pick apple
